#!/bin/bash
cd "$(dirname "$0")"
G=~/.grok/bin/grok
gen() { $G --always-approve -p "Read brief.md in this folder and follow its STYLE LOCK exactly. Generate ONE image (landscape 16:9) and save it as $1 in this folder. Scene: $2" > "log-$1.txt" 2>&1; }
gen s1-hero.png "the opening of the game: a broken weathered wooden pier with three missing planks at golden hour; a small rusty fishing boat rocks against it; four dock workers in hi-vis vests (orange, yellow, blue, green) carry tall wobbling stacks of blue fish crates across a tilting gangplank, the top crate of one stack is sliding off toward the water; across the bay in the distance a huge gleaming modern rival port with giant cranes and a neon sign reading 'GOLDBERG PORT'; seagull on a sign that reads 'PIER 1'." &
gen s2-ship-leaves.png "comedy moment: a small cargo boat is pulling away from the pier with its horn blowing, the gangplank has just dropped into the water; one worker in an orange vest is stuck on the departing deck surrounded by crates, arms up in despair; two friends sprint to the edge of the pier, one mid-jump; a crate floats in the water; the captain leans out of the wheelhouse laughing." &
gen s3-forklift.png "chaos on a concrete dock: a yellow forklift is tipping over the dock edge toward the harbour with a pallet of orange crates sliding off its forks; crates bursting, fish spilling onto wet concrete; one worker knocked flat and ragdolling; another worker holding a hand trolley stares in shock; corrugated warehouse shed and stacked containers behind." &
gen s4-storm.png "storm: dark sky, heavy rain and wind, waves crashing over the quay; workers in hi-vis vests and hard hats haul ropes to tie down a stack of containers; loose crates blowing along the pier and splashing into the sea; a small dockside crane swings a green container on its hook dangerously over the crew; harbour lights and a siren lamp glowing red." &
gen s5-night.png "cozy night between work days: the small harbour at night lit by warm sodium lamps and string lights; the pier now repaired with new planks and a small corrugated shed; four workers relax by the tea stall with steaming cups next to a big wall-mounted contract board with pinned ship contracts; a parked forklift; the rival port glows across the bay." &
gen s6-crane.png "later stage of the game: a mid-size cargo port, a player-operated dockside crane lifts a blue shipping container that swings toward the workers below, who dive out of the way; a medium container ship docked with colourful containers; forklifts moving pallets; the rival port across the bay now looks closer and a little worried." &
wait
